From: oded106e
Subject: [PATCH] luci-app-upnp: list nftables port maps that carry a counter
 
miniupnpd >= 2.3.10 built for nftables always adds a counter to its DNAT
rules (ENABLE_NFT_RULE_COUNTER), e.g.
 
  iif "wan" @nh,72,8 0x11 th dport 3074 counter packets 0 bytes 0 dnat ip to ...
 
The regex expects "dnat" right after the port, so no rule matches and the
Active Service Port Maps table stays empty. Skip whatever sits in between,
as openwrt/luci#8415 does.
 
The patch also adds a marker comment, so it can never be "already applied":
once LuCI changes this line the build stops - then delete this file.
---
diff --git a/applications/luci-app-upnp/root/usr/share/rpcd/ucode/luci.upnp b/applications/luci-app-upnp/root/usr/share/rpcd/ucode/luci.upnp
index f72b57b..737dadc 100644
--- a/applications/luci-app-upnp/root/usr/share/rpcd/ucode/luci.upnp
+++ b/applications/luci-app-upnp/root/usr/share/rpcd/ucode/luci.upnp
@@ -67,7 +67,10 @@ const methods = {
 
 			if (nft) {
 				for (let line = nft.read('line'), num = 1; length(line); line = nft.read('line')) {
-					let m = match(line, /^\t\tiif ".+" @nh,72,8 (0x6|0x11) th dport ([0-9]+) dnat ip to ([0-9.]+):([0-9]+)/);
+					// LOCAL FIX (oded106e fork, patches/feeds/edma-nss/luci/9001-*): skip the
+					// counter miniupnpd adds. Upstream openwrt/luci#8415 makes the same change;
+					// once LuCI has it this patch no longer applies and the build stops -> delete it.
+					let m = match(line, /^\t\tiif ".+" @nh,72,8 (0x6|0x11) th dport ([0-9]+).* dnat ip to ([0-9.]+):([0-9]+)/);
 
 					if (m) {
 						push(rules, {
 
